/-! # Étale multisections avoid nodes in regular nodal trait families

Source: Stacks Project, models.tex, Tags 0CDD and 0CDC; more-algebra.tex, Tag 0AP2.
The valuation argument is the extracted common-model step 8
(blueprint: lem-sfb-etale-sections-avoid-regular-nodes).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Every finite étale multisection of a regular nodal family over a DVR factors
through its relative smooth open subscheme. In particular every section does so.
The geometric fibres are reduced and pure of dimension one; connectedness is not
required. The nodal condition concerns nonsmooth closed geometric fibre points.

Source: Stacks Project, models.tex, Tags 0CDD and 0CDC; more-algebra.tex, Tag 0AP2
(blueprint: lem-sfb-etale-sections-avoid-regular-nodes).

Proof:
1. The fibre criterion (lem-trf-smooth-at-point-fibre-criterion) puts every point
   over the generic point in the smooth locus. At a nonsmooth special-fibre point,
   lem-sfb-trait-nodal-etale-dvr-model gives a pointed common étale chart with
   equation xy = pi^n over an étale DVR extension, n >= 1, preserving a uniformizer.
2. By lem-sfb-binomial-geometric-fibres and lem-sfb-dvr-binomial-local-geometry,
   that model is smooth off its special crossing. Apply the fibre criterion,
   lem-weil-pbc-etale-smooth-zero-dimensional-fibres, lem-trf-smooth-composition
   and lem-trf-etale-source-smoothness to see that the chart point maps to the origin.
3. By lem-sfb-etale-stalk-invariants regularity passes from W to the common chart
   and then to the model stalk. The regularity clause of
   lem-sfb-dvr-binomial-local-geometry forces n = 1.
4. Form T = B ×_W U. The residue-field tensor description of
   lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-points supplies a point above the selected points of
   B and U: the tensor product of two nonzero vector spaces over a field is nonzero.
   By lem-weil-pbc-etale-base-change-finite-limits and
   lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation, T is étale over the trait.
   Apply lem-sbc-etale-trait-stalk: its actual stalk D is a domain DVR, the structural
   map delta is injective, and its maximal ideal is generated by varpi = delta(pi).
5. The two pulled-back coordinates a,c lie in that maximal ideal and satisfy
   ac = varpi. Write a = varpi*a1 and c = varpi*c1. Since varpi is nonzero,
   cancellation gives 1 = varpi*a1*c1, contradicting properness of the maximal ideal.
   This is the elementary DVR calculation of def-sc-discrete-valuation-ring.
6. Every point of B therefore maps to the smooth open. Restrict the original map
   of structure sheaves to obtain its factorization through that open subscheme
   (def-weil-open-immersion). This works also for empty B. Take B = Spec R with
   its identity finite étale structure to obtain the section assertion.
-/
theorem etale_sections_factor_smoothLocus_of_regular_nodal
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsDiscreteValuationRing R]
    (W : Scheme.{u}) (f : W ⟶ Spec (.of R))
    [Flat f] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f]
    (hfib : ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω]
      (g : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ Spec (.of R)),
      IsReduced (pullback f g) ∧ (pullback f g).IsPureDimension 1)
    (hnodal : ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω]
      (g : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ Spec (.of R)) (z : pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g),
      z ∈ closedPoints ↥(pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g) →
      z ∉ (pullback.snd f g).smoothLocus →
        Nonempty
          (@AlgEquiv Ω
            (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((pullback f g).presheaf.stalk z))
              ((pullback f g).presheaf.stalk z))
            (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ω ⧸
              Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ω) *
                (MvPowerSeries.X 1 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ω)})
            _ _ _ ((pullback.snd f g).completedLocalScalarMap z).toAlgebra inferInstance))
    (hgeneric : Smooth (pullback.snd f
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap R (FractionRing R))))))
    (hregular : IsRegularScheme W) :
    (∀ (B : Scheme.{u}) (p : B ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsFinite p] [Etale p]
      (b : B ⟶ W), b ≫ f = p →
      ∃ lift : B ⟶ f.smoothLocus.toScheme, lift ≫ f.smoothLocus.ι = b) ∧
    (∀ s : Spec (.of R) ⟶ W, s ≫ f = 𝟙 (Spec (.of R)) →
      ∃ lift : Spec (.of R) ⟶ f.smoothLocus.toScheme, lift ≫ f.smoothLocus.ι = s) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
